 "floorplan_note": "wires-only parent: core in the middle (ROM-side words from the N pins cross only the upper slice row, hub / host words from the S pins only the lower one), two store slices below and two above it, the four fans along the W / E faces (E pair MY). Every parent net is leaf register -> wire -> leaf register (or slot pin); physical/qwen_kv_centre/seq_cluster_cut.py gives the cuts and the worst hop. r3 (10-13): leaves on the 43.2 um child lattice with >= 20 um channels everywhere (the kc2 plan had 10.8 um between the two fans of a side and between the store slices): fans at y 43.2 / 259.2, slices at x 172.8 / 302.4, core at (259.2, 172.8); W / E pin spans = fan origin + the fan leaf's own ranges. S-face hub / host words moved under the core (x 262.0..347.6; they crossed the centre channel in the kc2 plan, whose 0.585 cut had the core centred ON the cut line).",
 "slot_change_request": "el1013-qwen-kvcentre 10-13 (contract v4 slot `seq`, cell qkd_seq), posted in el1011-qwen-tp8.log: (1) pin list of the merged die: rf / tf / d2df / gq / gr / t_flt dropped (no producer / consumer on one die), ROM-side words on the N face: r_x3_d 524 + r_x3_cr, r_sd 56 (qfd_seq_su dc[55:0]), r_kvd 44, t_ar_d 520 + t_ar_cr, t_ds 187 (qfd_seq_su dh[186:0]), t_pw 75; quadrant words aq / kvn_d (+ kvn_<q>_cr in) / kc / af / mf on W (WS, WN) and E (ES, EN); hub ar / hf / hs and host hc 182 / tk 93 / kst 10 on S; (2) outline 604.8 x 475.2 (0.287 mm2; slot 777.576 x 518.376): the merged sequencer is ~48k flops in nine small leaves, and a store in the middle of a 778-um slot cannot reach both pin faces in one <= 500 um hop; (3) cluster layers: leaves M5, parent signals M6 / M7, PG M7 (the slot says cap M5).",
 "structural_change": "first build: cluster of nine hardened leaves (three masters) instead of one 55k-flop tile",
 "job": {
  "owner": "Claude:el1013-qwen-kvcentre",
  "branch": "claude/qwen-kvcentre-1013",
  "tag": "kc5",
  "purpose": "Qwen ROM TP8 track B: the merged-die KV sequencer on the contract slot `seq` as a wires-only cluster parent over nine hardened leaves (qkd_seq_core, 4 x qkd_seq_xs, 4 x qkd_seq_fan; each <= 15k sinks on its own root, every pin a register). No parent cell, no parent flop. See slot_change_request (pin list, outline 604.8 x 475.2, cluster layers).",
  "benches": [
   {
    "name": "seq_equiv_exact",
    "cmd": "bash physical/qwen_kv_centre/bench.sh {RUN}/bench/eq seq_equiv",
    "expect": "pass",
    "pass_regex": "^PASS kv_centre seq_equiv",
    "threads": 1,
    "peak_ram_gb": 2,
    "needs": [
     "iverilog"
    ],
    "note": "cluster qkd_seq (wires-only parent + core + 4 xs + 4 fan) == flat ot_qkvd_kv_seq_merged on every output bit of every cycle: 96,336 cycles, 160 layers (kvd launches), 49 decode steps through the stage stepper against a ROM-sequencer model (stage order, token / position, result checked) + one step per stepper fault kind, host program / descriptor writes checked on both copies, credit-true traffic on every bundle, every output bit seen at 0 and 1, per-quadrant row-credit protocol checked"
   },
   {
    "name": "seq_equiv_wire_mutant",
    "cmd": "bash physical/qwen_kv_centre/bench.sh {RUN}/bench/eqm seq_equiv mut",
    "expect": "fail",
    "fail_regex": "^FAIL kv_centre seq_equiv [0-9]+ mismatching",
    "threads": 1,
    "peak_ram_gb": 2,
    "needs": [
     "iverilog"
    ],
    "note": "OT_QKD_SEQ_MUT: the parent swaps two store slices on the E copies of the q word"
   },
   {
    "name": "seq_equiv_coverage_refusal",
    "cmd": "bash physical/qwen_kv_centre/bench.sh {RUN}/bench/eqc seq_equiv cov",
    "expect": "fail",
    "fail_regex": "^FAIL kv_centre seq_equiv coverage refused",
    "threads": 1,
    "peak_ram_gb": 2,
    "needs": [
     "iverilog"
    ],
    "note": "a run of 8 layers is refused: the pass needs the traffic counts and full toggle coverage"
   },
   {
    "name": "layer_cluster_exact",
    "cmd": "bash physical/qwen_kv_centre/seq_layer_bench.sh pos {RUN}/bench/lay cluster",
    "expect": "pass",
    "pass_regex": "^PASS qkd_seq_layer cluster runs=14 exact=14",
    "threads": 16,
    "peak_ram_gb": 64,
    "needs": [
     "verilator"
    ],
    "note": "the KV-end attention layer step as a whole decode step through the CLUSTER (Verilator, STACK=h): 7 vectors x VM stall 0 / 1 = 14 runs, all bit-exact against the golden; step 1,794 cycles at context 8192 (two-die 1,842); measured 10-13 on ot-agidock128"
   },
   {
    "name": "layer_cluster_wire_mutant",
    "cmd": "bash physical/qwen_kv_centre/seq_layer_bench.sh neg {RUN}/bench/layn wire cluster",
    "expect": "fail",
    "fail_regex": "^FAIL qkd_seq_layer cluster mutant wire detected",
    "threads": 16,
    "peak_ram_gb": 64,
    "needs": [
     "verilator"
    ],
    "note": ""
   },
   {
    "name": "layer_flat_qswap_mutant",
